- add INSTALL.bat (Windows) and install.sh (Linux/Bazzite) dependency
  installers plus requirements-dev.txt (pytest, pytest-asyncio, ruff,
  pandas, python-docx) so the full suite installs in one step
- add JARVIS.sh launcher: kernel 8170 + bridge 8171 + Orbit browser,
  detached via nohup, idempotent reuse of running services, token file
  at the same LOCALAPPDATA-or-~ fallback the Python components resolve
- orbit: cross-platform Chromium resolution (J_BROWSER_CHROMIUM_PATH >
  PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH/platform ms-playwright store incl.
  ~/.cache/ms-playwright > system chromium) in orbit/cdp.py and
  scripts/orbit_launch.py
- executor: sh/bash governed shell on POSIX with platform default shell,
  bash/sh -c argv, Windows-only creationflags via getattr, realpath-
  normalized cwd allow/deny lists (fixes /home -> /var/home symlink
  rejecting every home cwd on Fedora Atomic/Bazzite), POSIX system dirs
  in blocked defaults
- shell tool schema accepts powershell|cmd|sh|bash
- cli: read_line honors injected key sources on POSIX (headless/scripted
  input no longer falls through to stdin)
- bridge: wire the documented RAG injection into the _chat funnel and add
  the documented JARVIS_RAG=0 gate — both were missing
- tests: green on Linux without weakening assertions (portable outside-
  root dest paths, system-monitor cache isolation, hermetic playwright
  parent-module injection, POSIX-safe raw command quoting)
- docs: Linux/Bazzite notes in AGENTS.md

