+## Linux / Bazzite Notes
+
+- `install.sh` installs runtime + dev dependencies into `./venv`
+  (`requirements.txt` + `requirements-dev.txt`); `./install.sh --playwright`
+  also pulls unbranded Chromium into `~/.cache/ms-playwright`.
+- `JARVIS.sh` is the Linux launcher (kernel 8170 + bridge 8171 + Orbit
+  browser detached via nohup); state/logs/token in `~/JARVIS/` (same
+  `LOCALAPPDATA or ~` fallback the Python components resolve).
+- Chromium resolution is cross-platform: `orbit.cdp._find_chromium` checks
+  `J_BROWSER_CHROMIUM_PATH` > `PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH` / platform
+  ms-playwright store (`~/.cache/ms-playwright` on Linux) > system
+  `chromium` on PATH / standard locations.
+- Governed shell defaults to `sh` on POSIX (`powershell` on Windows);
+  raw `shell.execute` commands run via `bash -c`/`sh -c` on Linux.
+  Tool schema accepts `shell: powershell|cmd|sh|bash`.
+- Bazzite (immutable Fedora): no root needed for repo + venv in `$HOME`;
+  layer Python/Node with `rpm-ostree install ...` (reboot once) or use a
+  toolbox/devcontainer when system python3 < 3.11.
+
 ## Code Style
 
 - No comments unless asked.
